[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition is a 3/4 overhead view at a 40-degree angle, showing two individual plates of whole-grain toast side-by-side, with the foreground plate in sharp focus and the background plate softened by a shallow depth of field. The scene features four thick, golden-brown toasted slices of whole-wheat bread, spread with a generous, chunky, vibrant bright-green mash of smashed peas, Greek yogurt, and finely flecked fresh mint. Resting on top of the pea-smeared toast are soft, fluffy, pale-yellow scrambled eggs in distinct, delicate curds, sprinkled with snowy-white crumbles of feta cheese. Next to the toasts on each plate, a small pile of freshly sliced, deep-red, glossy strawberry halves sits directly on the ceramic surface. The plates are simple, matte white ceramic. The setting is a rustic, aged oak wood table with visible grain and small, scattered crumbs from the toasted bread. Props include a single stainless steel fork with a wooden handle resting casually beside one plate and a small, rustic ramekin containing a few remaining whole green peas blurred in the background. Lighting is soft, directional natural light from a window on the left, creating gentle shadows and highlighting the moisture on the strawberries and the creamy texture of the pea mash. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene captures a lived-in, warm, authentic home kitchen atmosphere. Included are slight natural imperfections: a tiny, stray green pea on the table, a slight oil sheen on the scrambled eggs, and crumbs scattered unevenly across the wood. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces."
]
